# Prettier formats every file type it supports here, because the text lint job
# (cboone/gh-actions lint-text.yml) runs `prettier --check .`. This file is what
# keeps that from reaching anything nobody here authors, or anything that must
# not change.

# Preserved verbatim as the source brainstorm the build plan grew from.
# Reformatting it would edit a historical record, and Prettier would: run with
# this file bypassed (`--ignore-path /dev/null`), it flags the brainstorm.
# `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc` ignores the same directory for the same reason; the
# two lists are kept in step by hand, because neither tool can read the other's.
docs/design/

# npm writes this file, so its layout is npm's to decide and no formatter should
# be judging it. Prettier 3.9.6 does not flag it today (measured 2026-09-14);
# the entry stops a future npm or Prettier release from turning a lockfile
# update into a formatting failure.
package-lock.json

# Prettier already skips `node_modules/` with no configuration. It is listed
# because the reader's question is whether a dependency's files can be
# reformatted, and an empty answer is not one.
node_modules/

# Build outputs and working material. Nothing here is authored. Prettier also
# honours .gitignore, which covers these already; they are named so this file
# answers the question on its own.
build/
zig-out/
zig-pkg/
.zig-cache/
dist/
verification/
